    "q-15819": {
      "dom_id": "step-q15819",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "If $y=|x|+2$, what are the coordinates of the minimum point on the graph?",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that $y=|x|+a$ is a vertical translation of the absolute value graph $y=|x|$ by $a$ units up.\n\nThe function $y=|x|+2$ has $a=2.$ Therefore, it is a vertical translation of the absolute value graph $y=|x|$ by $2$ units up.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14192632/assets/47bab8c5a2fa41bbe03dd6d5ed8d3c4a7d005e3cbb0eefdd258ff0ecbd61ee5c.png)\n\nLooking at the graph, we can see that the coordinates of the minimum point are $(0,2).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
