    "q-3677": {
      "dom_id": "step-q3677",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14192632/assets/6e662d75baca8ed3220915e3ff47daf32c4d25c34933a0188e29c404664273c7.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the curve shown above?",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the graph of $y=|x-a|$ is a horizontal translation of the absolute value graph $y=|x|$ by $a$ units right.\n\nHere, the graph is moved *right* by $2$ units. This corresponds to $a=2.$ So, the equation of the graph is $y=|x-2|.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14192632/assets/3c305a89fe9fd400cd9c58cfb12522b143b2654a49fa58aee582ba1100f94daa.png)",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-3677-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "y=2|x|",
